    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0179" n="1013" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1013"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/182b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Representatives
                        in Latin American Countries </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 7, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Enemy trading list and all corrections, additions, removals are to be made
                    public. You will take appropriate action and so instruct consuls your
                    jurisdiction, furnishing them list and subsequent information.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d110-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="1" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>In the telegrams to some of the countries notice of changes in the enemy trading
                    list was included.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
